hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16714","He said: Hajjaj narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Abu al-Khayr, that Junada ibn Abi Umayya narrated to him that men from the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), some of them said: Emigration has ended, and they differed about that; he said: So I set out to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, people say emigration has ended; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Emigration does not end so long as jihad remains."
